 "details": {
  "title": "My One and Only Love",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Johnny Hartman’s record in his key, C (D for the trumpet), concert G3 to D5. It plays in that guitar track’s time, about 63, slowing at the end. It keeps Hartman’s ways: the long A let go before the guitar’s line, G held in the bridge where the guitar holds C♯ minor 7♭5 for him, and his slow ending, the last phrase stretched over the falling chords, C over the suspended G, F♯ and G before he lands on C, and C held into F minor 6 over C. A short line leads in, D, C, B, A♭ over the G chords, and the trumpet closes with C major 9 rising to its D.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Guy Wood and Robert Mellin (1952)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, as Johnny Hartman sings it on his record with John Coltrane, on the Fret Finder page’s chords"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "C major concert (D for the trumpet), Hartman’s key"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Two bars on G, A A bridge A, a slow ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (moaol-guitar.mp3), 2:52"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The two intro bars come first, so bar 1 of the Fret Finder page is bar 3 here"
   ]
  ]
 }
